WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.010
Fake claim and migration messages often borrow familiar project names. Beacon helps readers

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:10.020
inspect the actual link before connecting a wallet. It works without asking the

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:15.030
project team to register. These are real screenshots from the public prototype, with

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.186
synthetic attack examples.

00:00:17.686 --> 00:00:22.029
Open the application and paste a URL or a Discord message. No account

00:00:22.029 --> 00:00:26.372
or wallet is needed to inspect a link. Analysis stays in the browser.

00:00:26.372 --> 00:00:30.715
The application does not upload the message or visit the target website. Each

00:00:30.715 --> 00:00:32.719
extracted link receives its own result.

00:00:34.219 --> 00:00:38.717
The official host example matches a dated reference sourced from public Arkiv pages.

00:00:38.717 --> 00:00:43.215
This result means an exact host match, not that a campaign or wallet

00:00:43.215 --> 00:00:47.713
signature is safe. The evidence panel identifies a live Arkiv record from the

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:52.211
Beacon curator. The curator reference is sourced independently; it is not an endorsement

00:00:52.211 --> 00:00:53.595
from the Arkiv team.

00:00:55.095 --> 00:01:00.613
Now inspect the synthetic impersonation example. The words arkiv dot network appear inside

00:01:00.613 --> 00:01:06.132
a longer, unrelated host. Beacon exposes that destination and explains the misleading subdomain.

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:11.651
The warning is based on visible URL structure, without opening the potentially dangerous

00:01:11.651 --> 00:01:12.075
page.

00:01:13.575 --> 00:01:18.967
A disguised Markdown link shows an official address while pointing somewhere else. Beacon

00:01:18.967 --> 00:01:24.358
compares the visible label with the actual target and highlights the difference. It

00:01:24.358 --> 00:01:29.750
also checks Unicode names, embedded credentials, shorteners and possible redirect parameters. Unknown does

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.408
not automatically mean scam.

00:01:32.908 --> 00:01:37.928
The open source implementation includes thirty nine passing tests and a documented Arkiv

00:01:37.928 --> 00:01:42.948
schema. Eight real records are now published on Tiramisu. Independent creator-filtered reads return

00:01:42.948 --> 00:01:47.968
seven; the impersonation record is excluded even after ownership is transferred to the

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:52.988
curator. Public receipts make these writes reproducible. No live threat feed or automatic

00:01:52.988 --> 00:01:58.008
Discord bot is connected. Try Beacon at beacon arkiv dot vercel dot app.
